# Failed-request dumps from --dump-failures contain FULL PROMPTS, including
# the operator's CLAUDE.md and any file contents the agent read. Never commit.
fail-*.json

# Local environment / credential files. Hosted-arm credentials such as
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY are read from the environment; a developer may keep them in
# a local .env. Never commit real values. .env.example (placeholders) stays
# tracked so the variable names stay documented.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# Agent benchmark raw data IS tracked -- results.jsonl and the run logs.
# Each row is hours of wall time that cannot be cheaply regenerated, and rows
# carry their own environment capture, so old runs stay interpretable.

# #133: the run lock is a claim on ONE machine, not a fact about the repo.
# Syncing it would let a lock taken on the M5 Max wedge the Linux tier.
.run-lock.json
# results.ledger_lock: the sibling lock every ledger append and rewrite holds.
# Empty, per machine, and never evidence.
*.jsonl.lock
*.json.lock

# The harness's own checkouts of the target repositories (#146).
#
# The agent's export is built from these, never from the operator's working
# copies in ~/git. Before this, a run renamed ~/git/monitor aside and stood an
# export in its place -- so the only usable checkout was one the operator had
# no reason to know was load-bearing. On 2026-09-04 he committed in it for
# twenty minutes and five trials recorded an escape that never happened.
#
# Cloned by scripts/sync_sandbox_targets.py; safe to delete and re-create.
sandbox/

# Peer bookkeeping state lives in ~/.local-llm-bench now (#238)
.claude/peer/

# summarize.py tees a machine-specific log on every invocation, and
# test_summarize.py invokes it end to end -- so a plain `pytest` run used to
# leave artifacts in hardware/<machine>/logs/, and twelve were committed before
# anyone noticed. The test now removes the file it caused; this is the backstop,
# because summarize is a read-only reporting script whose output is regenerable
# and carries nothing a result row does not.
hardware/*/logs/summarize-*.log

# report.py is the same class of script and was missed: read-only, its output
# regenerable from the ledger, carrying nothing a result row does not. Every
# invocation tees a machine log, so simply ASKING what the numbers say left the
# tree dirty -- and a dirty tree is what the pre-launch check refuses on, so a
# reporting command could block the next measurement or get committed as noise.
# hardware-id and hf-sweep logs ARE tracked and stay that way: those record a
# machine fact or an outside observation at a moment, neither of which can be
# regenerated later.
hardware/*/logs/report-*.log

# decode_ab.py's default output dir (scripts/decode_ab.py). Per-rep CSVs and
# logs from a paired decode A/B -- scratch that a later run overwrites, and the
# result is quoted on the issue, never committed. Left untracked it makes
# `git status` dirty and sets harness_dirty on the next run's rows (#48).
benchmarks/ds4/decode-ab/

# Agent fork worktrees (git worktree add under .claude/); scratch, never tracked.
.claude/worktrees/

# GitHub Pages build output (scripts/clock_cap_site.py and the pages workflow)
_site/

# #1404: video files never belong in this public repo. The video-gen reference
# clips are the operator's own videos and can carry a GPS tag; they and their
# frames live in ~/bench-logs/videogen/. scripts/videogen/ refuses an output
# path inside any git work tree, the refuse-video-files pre-commit hook refuses
# a forced `git add -f`, and tests/test_no_media_files.py reads the bytes of
# every tracked file. These rules keep them out of `git status` and `git add .`.
# Bracketed so that IMG_0001.MOV, .Mp4 and every other case match too.
*.[mM][pP]4
*.[mM][oO][vV]
*.[mM]4[vV]
*.[mM][kK][vV]
*.[wW][eE][bB][mM]
*.[aA][vV][iI]
*.[hH][eE][iI][cC]
*.[hH][eE][iI][fF]
*.[aA][vV][iI][fF]
*.3[gG][pP]
*.[mM][tT][sS]
*.[mM]2[tT][sS]
*.[hH][eE][vV][cC]
*.[yY]4[mM]
# Frames never sit beside the prompts: only JSON belongs in benchmarks/videogen/.
benchmarks/videogen/**/*.[jJ][pP][gG]
benchmarks/videogen/**/*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
benchmarks/videogen/**/*.[pP][nN][gG]
benchmarks/videogen/**/*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]
benchmarks/videogen/**/*.[gG][iI][fF]
benchmarks/videogen/**/*.[bB][mM][pP]
benchmarks/videogen/**/*.[tT][iI][fF]
benchmarks/videogen/**/*.[tT][iI][fF][fF]
